; A PLAIN loose-list mint (`[* bar]` over a non-exposable element) synthesizes the wasm wrapper
; class `BarList`; a user rule of a DIFFERENT shape (`bar_list = tstr`) snake_case-claims that same
; ident. Under --wasm=true both would be defined in `wasm/src/generated/mod.rs` — the user `pub type
; BarList = String;` alias and the synthesized `pub struct BarList(...)` wrapper — an E0428 the
; generator formerly emitted at exit 0 (a silent miscompile). The generation-time duplicate-ident
; backstop at the `generated_files` seam owns this class: it scans the emitted `src/generated/**`
; source and rejects gracefully. Unlike the NonEmpty siblings (`non_empty_loose_builder_name_claimed`
; et al.), the plain loose/table families have NO IR-level collision scan — the emission-observing
; backstop is the pinned layer for them.
bar = [x: uint]
bar_list = tstr
holder = { xs: [* bar] }
